sequenceDiagram
    participant ReqA as Request A (POST)
    participant ReqB as Request B (POST, concurrent)
    participant Mutex as writeLock (async-mutex)
    participant Repo as DBDataRepository
    participant CSV as csv/data.csv

    ReqA->>Repo: create(dataA)
    Repo->>Mutex: runExclusive(...)
    ReqB->>Repo: create(dataB)
    Repo->>Mutex: runExclusive(...) [queued]

    Mutex-->>Repo: lock granted to A
    Repo->>CSV: read all rows
    Repo->>Repo: sanitize + check duplicate
    Repo->>CSV: write all rows (A included)
    Repo->>Mutex: release lock

    Mutex-->>Repo: lock granted to B
    Repo->>CSV: read all rows (already includes A)
    Repo->>Repo: sanitize + check duplicate
    Repo->>CSV: write all rows (A + B)
    Repo->>Mutex: release lock

    Note over ReqA,ReqB: Read-modify-write on the CSV file is serialized<br/>per repository instance, preventing lost updates<br/>between concurrent create / update / remove calls.
